I added three hooks in `.kiro/hooks/` and a "Hooks" section to `README.md`. The section is a table under "How Kiro was used", just before "Architecture". All three files parse as valid JSON and contain no secrets. I haven't watched them fire in Kiro, and I wrote the hook format from memory without checking it against the Kiro docs.

Each hook runs when a matching file is saved and asks the agent to do the check:

| File | Runs on save of | What the agent does |
|---|---|---|
| `lint-typecheck-on-save.kiro.hook` | `src/**/*.ts`, `src/**/*.tsx` | Runs `pnpm exec eslint <saved file>` and `pnpm typecheck`, then makes the smallest fix for errors the change introduced. It also keeps `src/core/` free of React and DOM imports and blocks `NEXT_PUBLIC_LLM_*`. |
| `core-unit-tests-on-save.kiro.hook` | `src/core/**/*.ts` | Runs the saved file's `*.test.ts` and `*.prop.test.ts` files with Vitest. If a test fails, it fixes the source for a bug or updates the test for an intended change. It never weakens a property from `design.md`. |
| `i18n-key-parity-on-save.kiro.hook` | `src/core/i18n/**`, `src/ui/i18n/**` | Runs the existing parity test in `src/core/i18n/i18n.test.ts`. It also compares `en.ts` directly with `zh-cn.ts` and `zh-tw.ts` for missing or extra keys and mismatched placeholders, and adds missing translations without removing any `en` key. |

Things you should know:
- **No separate strings folder:** this repo has no `src/i18n`. The UI strings live in `src/core/i18n/messages/`, so the third hook watches that folder plus `src/ui/i18n/`.
- **Chinese means both variants:** I read "zh" as both `zh-CN` and `zh-TW`. The existing test also covers `ja` and `ko`.
- **Overlap in `src/core/`:** saving a file there runs both the lint/typecheck hook and the tests hook.
- **Files I left alone:** `logs/t22-hooks.log` and `prompts/t22-hooks.md` were already untracked in the repo, so I didn't touch them.

